1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,840
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:03,270
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,380
(Episode 34)

4
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:10,680
Mi Mi.

5
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:14,890
I know how...

6
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:17,360
you feel.

7
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:18,660
No.

8
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:21,460
You don't know, Mother.

9
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:25,300
I know that you're not
just upset about Da Mi.

10
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:27,930
I really do understand.

11
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:34,210
I'm sorry.

12
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:39,240
Seeing that wretched fool
living like a stray dog...

13
00:00:40,510 --> 00:00:43,620
in that dingy semi-basement rental,

14
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:45,850
I couldn't help being his mother,

15
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:49,350
so I kept dropping off food...

16
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:52,790
for him to eat.

17
00:00:54,630 --> 00:00:56,090
I truly...

18
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:01,030
did you wrong, Mi Mi. I did.

19
00:01:06,810 --> 00:01:07,810
Mi Mi.

20
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,310
We're in big trouble.

21
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:40,510
To my dearest Mom...

22
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:42,140
Mom,

23
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:45,510
you're already having a hard time
with my brothers,

24
00:01:45,710 --> 00:01:47,780
so I'm sorry
for adding to your worries...

25
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:50,580
by quitting my department store job
without telling you.

26
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:53,350
Like I told you, I found a new job.

27
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:56,690
The commute from home
would be way too far,

28
00:01:57,060 --> 00:01:58,760
so I decided to move out on my own.

29
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:04,660
Moving out, dating someone,
and marrying a good guy...

30
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:06,830
has always been your wish for me.

31
00:02:07,570 --> 00:02:09,700
I want to give that my all.

32
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:12,800
There's no other reason,
so don't worry about me.

33
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:17,080
I've always been grateful to you.

34
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:20,850
Thank you so much
for raising me so well.

35
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:25,320
I'll definitely succeed
and repay you for all you've done,

36
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:28,820
so please stop worrying about me...

37
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:33,960
and start living for yourself.

38
00:02:34,590 --> 00:02:36,290
Buy yourself
some pretty clothes, too.

39
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,370
You little brat.

40
00:02:41,770 --> 00:02:44,370
Moving out
with just a single letter?

41
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:47,670
Did she really think...

42
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:50,940
I wouldn't see right through her?

43
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,360
Mi Mi,

44
00:03:09,930 --> 00:03:13,970
I already took my medicine today.
You don't have to get it for me.

45
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:16,900
All right.

46
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:22,070
Leave it.

47
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:24,010
I'll do it.

48
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:26,640
All right.

49
00:03:29,310 --> 00:03:30,320
Mi Mi.

50
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:45,200
Mrs. Choi, why is my sister
taking so long to come out?

51
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:46,930
Is she feeling unwell again?

52
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:49,800
Mi Mi.

53
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:51,240
Leave her be.

54
00:03:51,970 --> 00:03:54,710
I'll go and watch
the restaurant right now.

55
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:05,720
Wait. Come to think of it,

56
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,350
she really hasn't been
looking well lately.

57
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:14,560
Mi Mi. This won't do.

58
00:04:14,930 --> 00:04:16,560
Come with me
to Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine...

59
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:19,360
Mi Mi.

60
00:04:24,670 --> 00:04:25,670
Mi Mi.

61
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:29,070
No matter how upset you are
with the kids,

62
00:04:29,510 --> 00:04:31,380
and no matter how hurt you are
by Mrs. Choi,

63
00:04:31,710 --> 00:04:32,980
this is going too far.

64
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:34,810
Why are you the one moving out?

65
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:37,580
Kick the kids out instead
if you must.

66
00:04:37,650 --> 00:04:40,080
This is your house, remember?

67
00:04:42,190 --> 00:04:43,290
Who said I was leaving?

68
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:47,490
Aren't you packing to move out?

69
00:04:48,230 --> 00:04:49,590
It certainly looks like it.

70
00:04:57,140 --> 00:04:59,800
Wait, this is all my stuff.

71
00:05:01,110 --> 00:05:02,410
Am I coming with you?

72
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:04,510
Are you taking me along?

73
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:07,750
You're getting out of my house.

74
00:05:08,010 --> 00:05:11,320
Why?
Why are you taking it out on me?

75
00:05:11,750 --> 00:05:12,980
You really have to ask?

76
00:05:13,690 --> 00:05:16,950
Don't tell me Da Mi said...

77
00:05:17,190 --> 00:05:20,960
she was moving out because of me?

78
00:05:21,490 --> 00:05:24,230
No way. She really ratted me out.

79
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:27,870
- Right?
- You just blew your own cover.

80
00:05:28,170 --> 00:05:29,500
I never said a thing.

81
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:31,640
What cover?

82
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:37,410
What on earth did she write
in that letter?

83
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:46,520
Mi Mi.

84
00:05:48,190 --> 00:05:50,760
Now that you know,
take this bag and get out.

85
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:54,390
What are you waiting for?

86
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:56,460
Mi Mi.

87
00:05:57,030 --> 00:05:59,000
Come on, this is too much.

88
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:02,630
You're practically a parent to me.

89
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:06,740
How could you kick out
your only sister?

90
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:09,210
Ever since Mom and Dad died early,
up until this day,

91
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:12,180
I've raised you in their place
and cleaned up every mess you made.

92
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:15,880
But didn't I warn you?

93
00:06:16,050 --> 00:06:17,650
Whoever makes Da Mi
shed a single tear,

94
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:20,320
no matter who they are,
they're dead to me.

95
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:23,090
Even if it's you,
I'll never see you again.

96
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:28,030
Are you really kicking me out?

97
00:06:28,590 --> 00:06:29,590
Yes.

98
00:06:30,630 --> 00:06:32,800
No, I can't leave. Absolutely not.

99
00:06:34,370 --> 00:06:38,240
You know I don't even have
1,000 dollars to my name.

100
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:39,600
My paycheck...

101
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:42,470
You know Mrs. Choi handles
all of it.

102
00:06:43,170 --> 00:06:45,580
Please, Mi Mi,
just forgive me this once.

103
00:06:45,810 --> 00:06:47,080
Just this one time.

104
00:06:47,410 --> 00:06:48,650
I'm begging you.

105
00:06:48,810 --> 00:06:50,520
Don't kick me out.

106
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:52,080
You have nowhere to go?

107
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:53,680
And no money?

108
00:06:53,790 --> 00:06:56,890
No, I don't have a cent.

109
00:06:56,950 --> 00:06:59,220
- Then...
- Just tell me, Mi Mi.

110
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,260
I'll do anything.

111
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:01,760
Should I get down
on my knees and beg?

112
00:07:01,990 --> 00:07:05,100
Or write an apology letter
like back then?

113
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:08,600
Forget that.
Bring my daughter back. Right now.

114
00:07:09,770 --> 00:07:12,640
Wait, Mi Mi. Where are you going?

115
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:15,910
To work, obviously. Did you forget?

116
00:07:16,340 --> 00:07:17,440
Not only is this house mine,

117
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:18,540
but the restaurant is
also under my name.

118
00:07:18,810 --> 00:07:19,810
Mi Mi.

119
00:07:19,910 --> 00:07:21,950
Where on earth
am I supposed to find her?

120
00:07:22,010 --> 00:07:23,480
How could I?

121
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:25,380
Figure it out.

122
00:07:26,180 --> 00:07:27,290
Mi Mi.

123
00:07:28,250 --> 00:07:29,320
Mi Mi.

124
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:32,160
Seriously, what do I do?

125
00:07:34,390 --> 00:07:35,590
Jo Ri Ja.

126
00:07:36,330 --> 00:07:39,100
You've really cooked your own goose.
I must be out of my mind.

127
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:40,800
Seriously.

128
00:07:44,300 --> 00:07:46,300
Mother, you should have called.

129
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:48,810
I'd have come out to meet you.

130
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,910
What brings you here
so early in the morning?

131
00:07:52,010 --> 00:07:53,010
What brings me?

132
00:07:53,510 --> 00:07:54,680
Are you asking
because you don't know?

133
00:07:56,150 --> 00:07:57,480
Mother.

134
00:07:57,850 --> 00:07:59,650
Now that my sisters,
Mi Mi and Ri Ja, know everything,

135
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:01,590
and it's all out in the open anyway,

136
00:08:01,990 --> 00:08:03,920
could you please cut us some slack?

137
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:05,420
Since when are they your sisters?

138
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:07,690
And who here is your mother?

139
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,530
Even so, Mother...

140
00:08:14,230 --> 00:08:15,230
It's 10,000 dollars.

141
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:21,210
Ten thousand dollars?

142
00:08:21,470 --> 00:08:23,540
Even a flea has a sense
of shame, you know?

143
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:26,940
If you have an ounce
of human decency left,

144
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:29,650
take that money,
get out of our neighborhood,

145
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:30,780
and prove it.

146
00:08:35,690 --> 00:08:37,460
We don't need this money.

147
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:39,990
As for me, Mother,

148
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:42,430
even if it's late, I want to take
good care of you close by,

149
00:08:42,490 --> 00:08:44,660
and get along with the family.

150
00:08:44,660 --> 00:08:46,130
My husband wants that too.

151
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,600
So...

152
00:08:48,870 --> 00:08:51,640
you plan to stay put
in this neighborhood?

153
00:08:51,870 --> 00:08:53,840
Mom, when did you get here?

154
00:08:57,070 --> 00:08:58,080
What's going on?

155
00:08:58,610 --> 00:09:01,510
Is this creature
still working at the clinic?

156
00:09:01,810 --> 00:09:05,250
Honey, Mother is telling us
to move out.

157
00:09:05,650 --> 00:09:08,520
Even if it's late,
I just wanted to be close to Mother...

158
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:10,190
and take really good care of her.

159
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,390
Shut up...

160
00:09:11,790 --> 00:09:13,290
before I rip that big mouth
of yours open!

161
00:09:14,260 --> 00:09:16,430
"Big mouth"? Mom, really?

162
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:20,330
You still haven't quit?

163
00:09:20,830 --> 00:09:21,830
I told you.

164
00:09:21,830 --> 00:09:24,570
Quitting out of nowhere would put
Director Ju in a tough spot.

165
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:26,400
What?

166
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:29,810
Mother.

167
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:33,510
Let me show you
some pictures of Ye Ri.

168
00:09:34,010 --> 00:09:36,480
Our Ye Ri grew up so well.

169
00:09:36,650 --> 00:09:38,580
She's doing great
at her company too.

170
00:09:38,680 --> 00:09:42,090
The CEO of that huge company
adores our Ye Ri so much.

171
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:44,660
Who asked?

172
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:48,160
Mother, please don't be like this,

173
00:09:48,230 --> 00:09:49,790
and just take a look
at your granddaughter's face.

174
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:50,860
Please, Mother?

175
00:09:50,930 --> 00:09:52,200
I told you to get that away from me.

176
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:55,000
Mother.

177
00:09:56,770 --> 00:09:58,870
It's Ye Ri. Kang Ye Ri.

178
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:04,840
Isn't she pretty?

179
00:10:05,380 --> 00:10:06,880
She inherited her brains
from you and my husband,

180
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:08,310
so she's incredibly smart.

181
00:10:09,410 --> 00:10:12,820
Last time,
Ye Ri couldn't greet you properly.

182
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:15,790
Ye Ri thought her grandmother
passed away early...

183
00:10:15,850 --> 00:10:19,320
I suppose you told her I died.
Keep it that way.

184
00:10:21,130 --> 00:10:23,660
I told you to leave
this neighborhood.

185
00:10:24,530 --> 00:10:26,630
Wait... Mom.

186
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:28,100
Mother, wait a moment.

187
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:29,300
Mother.

188
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:36,240
No matter how dirt poor we may be,

189
00:10:36,810 --> 00:10:38,310
we can never take this money.

190
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:42,110
Mother, please see my sincerity.
Please?

191
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:50,490
Mom.

192
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:53,120
- Mom.
- Honey.

193
00:10:53,190 --> 00:10:54,190
Honey.

194
00:10:54,830 --> 00:10:55,830
Let her go.

195
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:03,970
What? Now you want
to treat my mother well?

196
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:07,000
Gosh, you should've been an actress.

197
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:09,340
I mean it.

198
00:11:09,910 --> 00:11:11,680
And you saw it earlier, didn't you?

199
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:15,180
Your mother stared
so intently at our Ye Ri's photo.

200
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:19,350
I told you, blood runs really deep.

201
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:35,600
It's Ye Ri. Kang Ye Ri.

202
00:11:37,070 --> 00:11:39,540
Blood really is something.

203
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:42,110
You can't fake it.

204
00:11:43,310 --> 00:11:44,780
Her eyes, her mouth...

205
00:11:45,210 --> 00:11:48,210
She looks just like Hak Sung
when he was little.

206
00:11:58,660 --> 00:11:59,720
Mi Mi.

207
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:04,500
I really want to bring
Da Mi back too.

208
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:08,230
But where do I even look for someone
who left on her own?

209
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:11,940
Right.

210
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:14,340
I have to find her
wherever she is, of course.

211
00:12:15,070 --> 00:12:16,810
I'll bring her back.

212
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:23,480
- Sir.
- Yes?

213
00:12:23,550 --> 00:12:27,850
How about a phone stand?
It's seven dollars for one...

214
00:12:28,150 --> 00:12:29,920
and 12 dollars for a pair.

215
00:12:30,050 --> 00:12:32,520
If you buy them,
I'll pour you some ginseng liquor...

216
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,290
on the house, okay?

217
00:12:34,390 --> 00:12:35,530
- Hey.
- You scared me.

218
00:12:35,590 --> 00:12:37,460
- What are you doing right now?
- I didn't do anything.

219
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:39,500
Wait a minute.

220
00:12:40,130 --> 00:12:42,500
- What?
- If your mom catches you...

221
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:45,700
doing stuff like this,
she'll skin you alive, you know?

222
00:12:47,610 --> 00:12:48,670
That's why...

223
00:12:49,410 --> 00:12:52,240
you should just look
the other way for me.

224
00:12:53,610 --> 00:12:57,350
Gang Nam, do you know
which company Da Mi joined?

225
00:12:58,950 --> 00:13:01,450
Of course I don't.
Do you, Aunt Ri Ja?

226
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:04,860
- Would I ask you if I knew?
- Right.

227
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:07,760
Text her quickly
and ask what her new company is.

228
00:13:08,430 --> 00:13:11,730
I'm busy right now. I'm swamped.

229
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:14,970
I need to sell
all 300 of these stands.

230
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:18,800
I'll help you sell them.
Hurry up and text her.

231
00:13:18,870 --> 00:13:21,210
No, ask her where she is right now.

232
00:13:21,370 --> 00:13:22,370
You mean it, right?

233
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:25,140
My phone...

234
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:28,210
Kkangda.

235
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:30,980
Where are you?

236
00:13:34,220 --> 00:13:35,650
(Hey, Kkangda, where are you?
I said, where are you?)

237
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,860
She read it. What a surprise.

238
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:40,890
What did she say? Where is she?

239
00:13:41,690 --> 00:13:42,690
What?

240
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:44,260
(Hey, Kkangda, where are you?
I said, where are you?)

241
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:45,560
Aunt Ri Ja.

242
00:13:46,330 --> 00:13:48,530
Kkangda left me on read.

243
00:14:05,250 --> 00:14:06,480
Focus.

244
00:14:09,690 --> 00:14:11,690
I heard the reception
for the show was good,

245
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:14,230
so what on earth is the problem
with you guys?

246
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:23,370
I really can't stand this.

247
00:14:32,410 --> 00:14:33,880
Goodness.

248
00:14:41,150 --> 00:14:42,150
Ms. Kang Da Mi.

249
00:14:46,060 --> 00:14:47,120
Yes?

250
00:14:50,260 --> 00:14:52,400
Is cleaning that up
important right now?

251
00:14:52,730 --> 00:14:54,570
Are you working
on the assignment I gave you?

252
00:14:55,270 --> 00:14:58,170
Finding and analyzing the materials
should take a few hours.

253
00:15:00,770 --> 00:15:02,570
You don't even know
how to prioritize. Unbelievable.

254
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:06,040
Head Designer Cha.

255
00:15:07,180 --> 00:15:08,180
Yes?

256
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:11,520
I really want to do a good job
on my assignment too.

257
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:13,220
There are lots of materials
to look up as well.

258
00:15:14,150 --> 00:15:19,120
However, the office is so cluttered
that I can't concentrate at all.

259
00:15:19,660 --> 00:15:21,990
I'll just tidy up for a moment
and get right to work.

260
00:15:22,790 --> 00:15:25,130
Could it be that you simply have
poor focus, Kang Da Mi?

261
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:29,200
Excuse me, but I find that hard
to agree with.

262
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:31,400
My concentration happens to be
quite high.

263
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:33,140
I'm not so sure.

264
00:15:35,970 --> 00:15:37,340
Head Designer Cha.

265
00:15:38,310 --> 00:15:40,680
- Yes?
- Admittedly, I keep my own room...

266
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:44,010
quite messy too.
Because that's my personal space.

267
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:47,220
However, this is an office
where we work.

268
00:15:47,550 --> 00:15:48,550
You use it, but as your assistant,

269
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:51,360
I share it with you.
It's a communal space.

270
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:54,990
A communal space, is it?

271
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:02,370
I'll step out for just a moment.
My hands got so dirty.

272
00:16:12,410 --> 00:16:14,610
Is it really that messy?

273
00:16:15,210 --> 00:16:16,910
I don't find it uncomfortable
at all.

274
00:16:28,030 --> 00:16:29,630
(Kang Dae Chi)

275
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:42,240
Wait, I'm the one
who should be crying.

276
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:44,440
Why are you crying?

277
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:47,780
Because I know
exactly how it feels...

278
00:16:48,150 --> 00:16:50,080
when your whole world
comes crashing down.

279
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:52,320
My money...

280
00:16:52,650 --> 00:16:54,120
I mean, how will you pay back...

281
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:57,290
Hwanggeum Capital now,
Mr. Kang Dae Chi?

282
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:00,290
You have a plan, right?

283
00:17:00,390 --> 00:17:02,290
About what you'll do
moving forward, I mean.

284
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:05,400
Please tell me
you have a plan, okay?

285
00:17:06,130 --> 00:17:08,930
You went to a top university.
You're extremely smart.

286
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:11,400
Besides, things like embezzlement
or breach of trust...

287
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,440
I figured you weren't the type...

288
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:13,640
to commit something
like that at all.

289
00:17:14,470 --> 00:17:16,710
That's why
I put all my trust in you.

290
00:17:22,610 --> 00:17:23,610
Right.

291
00:17:24,350 --> 00:17:26,420
I'm not that kind of guy,
so keep trusting me.

292
00:17:27,650 --> 00:17:29,320
It's true that I went
to a top university...

293
00:17:29,390 --> 00:17:31,660
and that my IQ is over 140,

294
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:36,090
but it's only been a few hours
since I got fired from my job.

295
00:17:37,860 --> 00:17:39,460
Could you please leave me alone?

296
00:17:40,030 --> 00:17:41,060
Ms. Cha Se Na.

297
00:17:44,270 --> 00:17:45,270
Then...

298
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:47,500
promise me just one thing.

299
00:17:47,810 --> 00:17:51,340
- I told you I'll pay you back.
- No, it's not about the money.

300
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:52,580
What is it now?

301
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:56,180
You must never go to the Han River.

302
00:17:56,850 --> 00:17:57,850
Understood?

303
00:17:59,150 --> 00:18:00,820
Why would I go to the Han River?

304
00:18:01,590 --> 00:18:02,820
I'm my grandma's grandson,

305
00:18:02,890 --> 00:18:04,820
and my mom's second son,
Kang Dae Chi.

306
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:08,530
What I mean is
I'm not going to break down here.

307
00:18:09,860 --> 00:18:10,930
You're not lying, right?

308
00:18:12,530 --> 00:18:14,730
Then let's pinky swear.

309
00:18:16,830 --> 00:18:17,870
Come on, give me your finger.

310
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:21,410
You're being so childish.

311
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:24,040
Fine.

312
00:18:29,150 --> 00:18:30,280
We have a deal, right?

313
00:18:33,050 --> 00:18:34,320
We need to seal it
with our thumbs too.

314
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:39,090
Sealed.

315
00:18:46,730 --> 00:18:48,470
(Sales by Item, Product, Month, Channel,
and Performance Analysis)

316
00:18:48,530 --> 00:18:49,530
(2026 Spring-Summer Sales by Item)

317
00:18:57,840 --> 00:19:00,310
Drink this and take your time
looking it over, Ms. Kang Da Mi.

318
00:19:01,210 --> 00:19:02,310
Thank you.

319
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:05,280
I only asked because I was lost,
but you went ahead...

320
00:19:05,350 --> 00:19:06,350
and found all the materials
I needed.

321
00:19:06,420 --> 00:19:07,780
Of course I should
help you find them.

322
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:10,690
Still, it feels like
the head designer...

323
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:13,190
gave his assistant too big a task
right from the start.

324
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:16,460
It's tough,
but I want to give it a shot.

325
00:19:18,730 --> 00:19:19,730
Here.

326
00:19:21,570 --> 00:19:24,740
These are last year's spring-summer
sales figures by category,

327
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:27,740
and this is the data
for this year's season.

328
00:19:28,310 --> 00:19:30,270
It'll help to compare them
side by side.

329
00:19:30,370 --> 00:19:33,380
And if you flip the page,
there are charts,

330
00:19:33,910 --> 00:19:35,610
which might make it easier
to see at a glance.

331
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:38,380
Okay.

332
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:42,120
Why is Team Leader Cha
being so nice to her?

333
00:19:43,990 --> 00:19:46,460
And why is she still here instead
of reviewing the materials...

334
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:47,790
in her own office?

335
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:55,230
Team Leader Cha.

336
00:19:57,530 --> 00:19:59,070
Feel free to ask me anything.

337
00:20:01,740 --> 00:20:02,970
Yes, Assistant Manager Kang.

338
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:06,310
Let's go check the samples
for the skirt and sneaker set...

339
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:07,810
launching in the first half
of next year.

340
00:20:07,950 --> 00:20:09,850
Is it that time already?

341
00:20:11,650 --> 00:20:14,380
We still have about ten minutes.
Hold on a moment.

342
00:20:15,020 --> 00:20:16,020
Da Mi.

343
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:20,320
This item here barely sold
all season long.

344
00:20:21,090 --> 00:20:22,530
It had the lowest sales figures.

345
00:20:23,160 --> 00:20:24,930
It was quite disappointing.

346
00:20:28,970 --> 00:20:30,670
(Product Planning Department)

347
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:33,800
- Ms. Kang Da Mi.
- Head Designer Cha.

348
00:20:33,870 --> 00:20:34,870
Yes.

349
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:37,340
What do you think
you're doing here right now?

350
00:20:38,540 --> 00:20:40,710
Team Leader Cha
found some data for me,

351
00:20:40,780 --> 00:20:42,250
so I was taking a quick look at it.

352
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:44,550
Is this your office?

353
00:20:45,320 --> 00:20:46,420
You were going to wash your hands,

354
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:48,320
so how can you disappear
for this long?

355
00:20:49,220 --> 00:20:50,250
Come back right now.

356
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:57,260
Let's go check the samples too,
Assistant Manager Kang.

357
00:20:57,860 --> 00:20:59,360
I'll get going now too.

358
00:21:11,780 --> 00:21:12,780
Ms. Kang Da Mi.

359
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:14,980
Yes, Assistant Manager Kang?

360
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:16,650
You should take this with you.

361
00:21:16,710 --> 00:21:18,120
(Product Planning Department)

362
00:21:18,180 --> 00:21:19,650
And going forward,
review your materials...

363
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:21,450
in the head designer's office.

364
00:21:22,550 --> 00:21:25,060
A head designer running around
looking for his assistant...

365
00:21:25,390 --> 00:21:26,890
isn't a good look.

366
00:21:28,830 --> 00:21:30,390
Yes, thank you.

367
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:36,070
You'd better watch yourself.

368
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:40,870
(Head Designer's Office)

369
00:22:09,800 --> 00:22:11,270
Well, no reaction.

370
00:22:13,570 --> 00:22:15,410
Pardon? What reaction?

371
00:22:15,870 --> 00:22:17,610
Nothing,
I was just talking to myself.

372
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:23,350
By the way, after spending
so much time in Product Planning,

373
00:22:23,410 --> 00:22:24,950
did you find the materials
you needed?

374
00:22:25,880 --> 00:22:27,750
Yes, Team Leader Cha helped me,

375
00:22:27,820 --> 00:22:29,390
so I brought them over,
and I'm going through them.

376
00:22:29,550 --> 00:22:31,590
That's good.
Finish looking through them.

377
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:33,690
I shared the task
because we're pressed for time.

378
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:39,560
By any chance,

379
00:22:41,130 --> 00:22:42,300
do you notice...

380
00:22:43,770 --> 00:22:45,040
anything different in here?

381
00:22:46,400 --> 00:22:47,840
Not really. Like what?

382
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:51,310
Never mind. Let's get back to work.

383
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:53,280
Back to work.

384
00:22:55,410 --> 00:22:57,450
I thought I walked
into the wrong office.

385
00:23:04,220 --> 00:23:05,390
Well...

386
00:23:06,690 --> 00:23:09,030
I have no idea
what you're muttering to yourself,

387
00:23:09,090 --> 00:23:11,390
but while we work together,
let's try to keep it down.

388
00:23:11,830 --> 00:23:13,030
It's a shared space.

389
00:23:15,930 --> 00:23:17,430
Yes, sir. I'm sorry.

390
00:23:30,580 --> 00:23:31,620
Da Mi,

391
00:23:31,850 --> 00:23:34,020
you can't just lie down
without washing up.

392
00:23:34,150 --> 00:23:35,590
At least change out of your clothes.

393
00:23:36,590 --> 00:23:40,320
I was looking forward to working
with a top designer,

394
00:23:40,790 --> 00:23:43,690
but this is no joke.
I'm so exhausted.

395
00:23:44,190 --> 00:23:45,660
It's just because
it's your first day.

396
00:23:46,460 --> 00:23:49,570
Still, you took a step closer
to your dream.

397
00:23:50,630 --> 00:23:52,700
I wonder if I can
even get any closer.

398
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:55,870
Oh, right.

399
00:23:58,280 --> 00:24:00,310
I forgot to eat dinner.

400
00:24:01,110 --> 00:24:02,450
Did you eat, Mi Seon?

401
00:24:03,910 --> 00:24:06,780
- Yes, I did.
- Are there any leftovers?

402
00:24:07,150 --> 00:24:08,420
Even ramyeon is fine.

403
00:24:09,350 --> 00:24:11,560
Just stay put.
I'll make you something.

404
00:24:12,620 --> 00:24:14,690
I could have gotten it myself.

405
00:24:24,800 --> 00:24:25,970
Rolled omelet.

406
00:24:26,370 --> 00:24:28,270
Next to Mom's,

407
00:24:28,340 --> 00:24:30,610
the rolled omelets you make
are seriously the best.

408
00:24:33,110 --> 00:24:34,510
Thank you for the food.

409
00:24:37,580 --> 00:24:38,980
Eat slowly.

410
00:24:41,790 --> 00:24:42,820
You'll get indigestion.

411
00:24:43,450 --> 00:24:44,450
This is so delicious.

412
00:25:13,120 --> 00:25:14,220
I have my own situation, but...

413
00:25:15,190 --> 00:25:18,150
Yes, Mother must be worried.

414
00:25:24,090 --> 00:25:26,900
Da Mi is at my place.
Come and take her home.

415
00:25:36,470 --> 00:25:37,510
Mi Seon.

416
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:41,750
Being here with you...

417
00:25:42,910 --> 00:25:44,550
feels so comfortable and nice.

418
00:25:46,250 --> 00:25:47,250
Pardon?

419
00:25:48,650 --> 00:25:50,750
I don't have to walk on eggshells...

420
00:25:51,450 --> 00:25:53,190
or worry about anything.

421
00:25:56,890 --> 00:25:58,190
Good night, Mi Seon.

422
00:26:01,930 --> 00:26:04,170
Sleep well, Da Mi.

423
00:26:16,980 --> 00:26:18,110
Aunt Ri Ja!

424
00:26:18,380 --> 00:26:20,920
- Aunt Ri Ja. Come look at this.
- What is it?

425
00:26:22,050 --> 00:26:25,190
I found out where Kkangda is.

426
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:27,390
What? Where?

427
00:26:27,790 --> 00:26:30,290
Not for free, you know.

428
00:26:31,190 --> 00:26:33,130
What? Seriously?

429
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:38,230
Fine. I'll let you sell
those phone stands to our customers.

430
00:26:38,540 --> 00:26:40,170
Where is she? Tell me, quickly.

431
00:26:45,210 --> 00:26:48,110
Please have some, Mother.

432
00:26:48,510 --> 00:26:50,780
You barely ate anything at dinner.

433
00:26:52,580 --> 00:26:55,420
I told you,
everything tastes like ashes.

434
00:26:57,750 --> 00:27:02,730
You have to take a bite first
so that she and I can eat too.

435
00:27:03,890 --> 00:27:04,890
Mother,

436
00:27:05,700 --> 00:27:09,870
do you know why I married your son?

437
00:27:11,130 --> 00:27:12,140
What?

438
00:27:13,900 --> 00:27:16,670
I fell for him
because he's such a dutiful son.

439
00:27:17,370 --> 00:27:20,140
Seeing how he always
treats you so well...

440
00:27:20,340 --> 00:27:21,750
truly warms my heart.

441
00:27:22,410 --> 00:27:26,020
Being by his side,
I learn so much from him too.

442
00:27:27,020 --> 00:27:29,250
Is that the truth?

443
00:27:29,990 --> 00:27:34,860
Did you really marry my son
just for that reason?

444
00:27:35,790 --> 00:27:37,660
Of course, Mother.

445
00:27:37,860 --> 00:27:41,360
Did you think I had
some other motive?

446
00:27:45,200 --> 00:27:49,470
So you wanted to know
why I married him,

447
00:27:50,310 --> 00:27:52,080
and that's why...

448
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:54,740
you had me investigated?

449
00:27:57,510 --> 00:27:58,520
What?

450
00:27:59,480 --> 00:28:00,480
Honey.

451
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:13,900
(Mission: Mompossible)

452
00:28:14,160 --> 00:28:16,570
While you're on this medication,
alcohol is off-limits.

453
00:28:16,700 --> 00:28:17,730
Ms. Jo.

454
00:28:17,830 --> 00:28:20,240
Dr. Ju, do you have feelings for me?

455
00:28:20,740 --> 00:28:23,770
If I hadn't met you
at the Han River that day,

456
00:28:23,840 --> 00:28:26,110
Kang Da Mi wouldn't exist today.

457
00:28:26,110 --> 00:28:27,140
I know that very well.

458
00:28:27,140 --> 00:28:28,950
What are you trying to tell me?

459
00:28:30,180 --> 00:28:32,150
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
